Z2  THE STATIC EDGE: positive density wherever the switch is partly on; no regular on->off solution
========================================================================================================
    x = X_0*(F(u) + Derivative(F(u), u)) + x_b   (from M_ph(<r) = F v_f^2 r/G:  4 pi G rho_ph/H^2 = X_0 d(F e^u)/du e^-u)
    lemma: where 0 < F < 1, x lies in the switch band (x > 0), so d(F e^u)/du > -x_b e^u/X_0: the enclosed phantom
    cannot decrease in baryon-poor outskirts while the switch is partly on
